meta {
  name: 14 Exam Schreiben names the chosen Aufgabe
  type: http
  seq: 14
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/centers/me/exam-sessions/{{b2ExamSessionId}}/results
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  Needs a candidate who has actually submitted the Schreiben block, so this
  is the last request and the one most likely to need setup: publish the
  sitting, add a participant, start it, submit SCHREIBEN with

    { "text": "...", "taskId": "{{b2SchreibenTaskA}}" }

  Then each attempt's schreibenSubmission.task should read
  "Aufgabe A — Bitte um Informationen", or Aufgabe B for the other.

  WHY IT MATTERS. The attempt recorded `exam-<modelltestId>`, naming the
  sitting rather than the prompt, so a trainer opened the marking screen with
  a letter and no way to tell which of two prompts it answered — while
  criterion I is exactly whether that prompt's required points were
  addressed.

  It also repaired the AI tier, and that part was broken for B1 too: the same
  placeholder was handed to the correction service as an exercise id, which
  cannot resolve it, so every AI-tier Schreiben suggestion was generated with
  no task in the prompt and no cap on criterion I. The model was asked to
  rate a letter without being told what the letter was supposed to say.

  A taskId from another Modelltest is refused — it is resolved within this
  paper, because the id arrives from the candidate's client.
}
